conio.c uses tcgetattr/tcsetattr/tcflush/TCSANOW but includes only <curses.h>
and <term.h>. ncurses' term.h does include <termios.h>, but only inside its
"#ifdef NCURSES_INTERNALS" block (term.h:93-151), so a normal consumer never
gets it: struct termios stays incomplete and the tc* functions are undeclared.

Reproduced against this ncurses: curses.h + term.h alone gives 4 errors
(incomplete struct termios, undeclared tcgetattr/tcsetattr, undeclared
TCSANOW); adding <termios.h> gives 0. Note this is not an API-level issue --
bionic declares all three at API 24, which is what we target.

--- a/src/console/conio.c
+++ b/src/console/conio.c
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@
 
 #include <curses.h>
 #include <term.h>
+/* ncurses only pulls <termios.h> in from term.h under NCURSES_INTERNALS. */
+#include <termios.h>
 
 #ifdef HAVE_SUN_OS
 #ifndef _TERM_H
